# DZQL - AI Quick Reference

## Core API Pattern (WebSocket)
```javascript
ws.api.get.{entity}({id})              // Single record
ws.api.save.{entity}({...data})        // Create/update
ws.api.delete.{entity}({id})           // Delete
ws.api.lookup.{entity}({p_filter})     // Autocomplete
ws.api.search.{entity}({filters, sort, page, limit})  // Search
ws.call('custom_function', {params})   // Custom functions
```

## Authentication
```javascript
await ws.call('login_user', {email, password});
// All operations auto-include user_id
```

## Graph Rules Variables
- `@user_id`, `@id`, `@field_name`, `@now`, `@today`
- `@before.field`, `@after.field` (in conditions)

## Path Syntax
```
@field->table[filter]{temporal}.target_field
```
- `$` in filter = current value
- `{active}` = temporal filtering

## Testing
```bash
bun venues:db          # Reset PostgreSQL
bun venues             # Start server
bun venues:test        # Run tests
bun venues:logs        # View logs
```

## Key Points
- Language: Plain JavaScript (NO TypeScript)
- FK includes: `{"field": "table"}` for derefs OR child arrays
- Deleted records throw "record not found" (not empty)
- Reset DB between test runs for isolation
- Server API requires explicit userId: `db.api.save.venues(data, userId)`
- Client API auto-injects userId: `ws.api.save.venues(data)`

